\DOC add_simps

\TYPE {add_simps : thm list -> unit}

\SYNOPSIS
Declare several theorems into the simp set.

\DESCRIBE
{add_simps thl} is {add_simp} for each theorem of {thl}, in one call and
with one extension of the term net. It is what to use for the clauses of
a definition, which come as a conjunction: {add_simps (CONJUNCTS th)}.

\FAILURE
Never fails.

\EXAMPLE
{
  # add_simps (CONJUNCTS count);;
  val it : unit = ()

  # length (simps ());;
  val it : int = 4
}

\SEEALSO
add_simp, add_type_simps, del_simp, simps.

\ENDDOC
